    <!-- H2: Practical applications -->
    <section>
      <h2 style="font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3.5vw, 2.1rem); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding-bottom: 12px; margin-bottom: 18px;">
        Practical applications: When counting days matters
      </h2>
      <p style="color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.75; font-size: 1.05rem;">
        Precise calendar counting is essential across diverse planning disciplines:
      </p>

      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; margin: 20px 0;" class="applications-grid">
        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px;">
          <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--accent); font-size: 1.15rem;">International Travel &amp; Visas</h3>
          <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6;">
            The European Schengen Area enforces a strict 90/180-day rule where non-EU visitors may not stay more than 90 days within any rolling 180-day window. Both entry and departure dates count toward the visa allowance (inclusive counting).
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px;">
          <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--accent); font-size: 1.15rem;">Project Delivery &amp; Sprints</h3>
          <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6;">
            Engineering managers use weekday totals to calculate sprint capacity and lead times. If a milestone spans 66 calendar days but only 48 weekdays, developer velocity must be budgeted against 48 production days rather than 66.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px;">
          <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--accent); font-size: 1.15rem;">Legal Notices &amp; Leases</h3>
          <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6;">
            Commercial contracts frequently specify 30, 60, or 90 days of written notice. Jurisdictions differ on whether the day of service counts, making accurate verification between exclusive and inclusive dates critical for compliance.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px;">
          <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--accent); font-size: 1.15rem;">Health &amp; Life Milestones</h3>
          <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6;">
            Obstetric pregnancy estimates are calculated as 280 days (40 weeks) from the first day of the last menstrual period. Similarly, personal fitness streaks and habit tracking rely on exact day-to-day tallies.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

